--- final message ---
I fixed most of the figure warnings for the two matplotlib figures, but `protocol_overview.png` is untouched. `paper.tex` recompiles cleanly to 14 pages, the same count as before. I did not re-run the validator, so the warnings below are not confirmed cleared.

**Changes**
- **Both matplotlib figures:** I edited `scripts/build_figures.py` and regenerated each as PDF plus a 300 DPI PNG. I also regenerated the `.prov.json` sidecars. `paper.tex` needed no edits, since it already references the PDFs.
- **`slope_interval_vs_decision_rule`:** I shortened the legend and annotation labels to "model, 4 seeds, 95% CI", "reference, 1 seed" and "CI straddles 0". The title font is now set to 10 pt, though this figure has no title.
- **`search_variants_descriptive`:**
  - The panel (a) series count is now 2 (per-seed points and mean) instead of 3. Both seeds share one colour, and the filled versus open marker still tells them apart.
  - The panel titles are 15 pt in the script, about 10 pt once the figure is scaled to text width.
  - The PNG is now 2523 px wide, up from 1618, so it clears the 2400 px full-width threshold.
  - I drew it at 8.5 inches with fonts scaled 1.5×, which keeps the rendered text at roughly 8–10 pt.
  - The y-axis label is now "censored runs" instead of "runs censored at step limit". The caption still says the runs are censored at the step limit.
- **`figure_manifest.json`:** I updated the title font sizes, series counts, font sizes and maximum label lengths to match the regenerated figures.

**Left unresolved**
- **`protocol_overview.png`:** Its "labels too long" and title-font warnings stay open. It is a raster concept figure from Autoillustrate with no plotting source here. I did not edit or upscale it.
- **Label-length warnings:** The check may still fire on the slope and search-variants figures. I don't know its threshold, and I picked the shorter labels without being able to test them against it.

I changed no scientific content or data.
